    "result_text": "I added an \"Export CSV\" button to the People section, and all 4 tests in `bin/e2e` now pass.\n\nPressing the button (`data-testid=\"export-people\"`) downloads `people.csv`. It has the header `name,grade,retired-from,due-total`, then one line per person in list order. Retired people are included even when \"show retired\" is off. Each line has the grade in force on the sheet's today, the retired-from date (empty if the person isn't retired) and the due-total as the People table shows it, including `n/a`. A value with a comma, a quote or a line break is wrapped in double quotes, with quotes inside doubled, and every line ends with a line feed.\n\nThe CSV is built in the browser from the data the screen already has, so the figures always match the table. Nothing changed in the server or the stored data, and exporting writes no audit record (the test doesn't expect one). The whole change is in `src/main/frontend/features/people/People.tsx`.\n\nMy first attempt never reached the code: I used a Python script to make the edit, and Python fails to start in this environment. That first test run was against the old app. I redid the edit with the editor, and the passing run above is of the real change.",
